# JetonBro mandatory Cursor operating rules

Cursor must read this entire file before planning, editing, running commands, or answering any implementation request in this repository.

After every accepted change, Cursor must update this file when the change affects architecture, invariants, state transitions, accounting, permissions, commands, deployment, or the current implementation status.

Cursor must never silently weaken, bypass, delete, or contradict a rule in this file. If a request conflicts with a rule, stop and explain the conflict before editing.

## Product boundary

JetonBro tracks virtual jetons used alongside physical games. Physical cards, physical money, hand evaluation, dealing, randomness, and payment processing are always outside the application.

Blackjack is the only implemented game until its full two-device flow is accepted. Poker and Zilch are future games, not reasons to build a generic rules engine now.

## Mandatory invariants

1. The server is authoritative for every balance and phase.
2. Every balance mutation creates an immutable ledger entry.
3. Every value-changing command is transactional and idempotent.
4. Ordinary bets and Insurance are separate locked-value accounts.
5. Normal box settlement never settles Insurance.
6. Insurance settlement never settles a normal box.
7. A round cannot complete while any box or Insurance bet remains unresolved.
8. A Player sees only their own boxes and balance.
9. A Player sees all their own open boxes together.
10. The permanent Player bottom area always shows their available value and jetons in every phase.
11. The Bank sees all active boxes.
12. The Bank phase label and transition action remain near the top.
13. Cards and real money are never represented, stored, transferred, or inferred.

## Blackjack phase sequence

`TABLE_SETUP -> BETTING -> PLAYING -> PAYOUT -> ROUND_COMPLETE -> BETTING`

No backward transitions and no phase skipping.

Insurance is a Bank-triggered window during PLAYING, not a phase. It is settled independently during PAYOUT.

## Accounting

- Unit: millijetons (`bigint`, 1000 = 1 jeton). Floating-point arithmetic is not used for balances.
- AVAILABLE is `TableMember.availableMillis`.
- LOCKED_BET is `BettingBox.lockedBetMillis`.
- LOCKED_INSURANCE is `InsuranceBet.amountMillis` until Insurance is settled.
- BANK_VIRTUAL_RESERVE is unlimited and not stored as a balance. It is the source of minted table jetons and payout profit, and the sink of lost ordinary and Insurance stakes.
- Commands that change value require an idempotency key and write at least one ledger entry in the same transaction.
- Ordinary payouts: win profit 1× / return 2×; push profit 0 / return 1×; loss return 0; Blackjack 3:2 profit 1.5× / return 2.5×; Blackjack 6:5 profit 1.2× / return 2.2×.
- Insurance 2:1: profit 2× Insurance stake / return 3× Insurance stake. Settled independently of the box.

## Permissions

- Owner: create table, invite, add/remove players before a round, assign Bank/Dealer, distribute jetons, archive later.
- Bank/Dealer: open betting, deal cards, Insurance window, payout phase, settle boxes, settle Insurance, start next hand.
- Player: own boxes only; bet/retract during BETTING; Double/Split during PLAYING; Insurance only while the window is open.

## Design architecture

- `classic` is the first and default skin.
- Game/domain logic must not import skin components or CSS.
- Skins must not contain permissions, accounting, phase rules, or payout calculations.
- Build shared semantic slots first, then render those slots through the active skin.
- A future skin must be replaceable without changing domain tests.
- Do not create per-skin copies of pages or game logic.

Recommended skin boundary:

```text
src/ui/core/                 semantic screen composition
src/ui/skins/classic/        Classic components, tokens and styles
src/ui/skins/registry.ts     typed skin selection
```

## Deployment

- One Next.js app, one PostgreSQL database.
- In-process SSE is single-instance only. Railway must run exactly one application instance.
- `GET /api/health` reports database connectivity and does not expose secrets.
- `npm run guardrails` before tests and build.
- `npm start` runs `prisma migrate deploy && next start`.
- Railway staging: `preDeployCommand` runs `npx prisma migrate deploy`, then `npx next start`, healthcheck `/api/health`, **exactly one replica**.
- `ALLOW_DEV_MAILBOX` is local/CI only and is ignored when `NODE_ENV=production`. `/api/dev/*` always 404s in production.
- Real email delivery requires `EMAIL_SERVER`. Without it, links are written to `tmp/mailbox.jsonl` only.

## Change discipline

Before editing:

1. Read this file.
2. Read the files and tests directly affected.
3. State the existing invariant or behavior being changed.
4. Keep the change within one vertical slice.

After editing:

1. Run focused tests.
2. Run the full test suite and production build before declaring a slice complete.
3. Render the affected 390x844 mobile states.
4. Verify at 320x700.
5. Update this file and the changelog when architectural facts or status changed.
6. Report exact results and genuine limitations.

Do not claim completion from code inspection alone.

## Current status

- Repository: Blackjack MVP staging baseline (not production-ready)
- Current game: Blackjack MVP
- Current skin: Classic
- Accepted references: `design/reference/classic/`
- Bank accounting: unlimited virtual reserve (`BANK_VIRTUAL_RESERVE`), not a stored Bank balance
- Verification: `npm run guardrails`, Vitest, `next build`, Playwright real-app phase screenshots plus two-session join
- Staging target: one Railway app replica, one PostgreSQL service, health `/api/health`, `ALLOW_DEV_MAILBOX=false`
- Production email SMTP delivery is not configured; invitation token generation is
- Next milestone: configure SMTP and magic-link cookies on staging, then archive/change-game UX. Do not enable GitHub automatic production deployment yet.
